.TH BIOSEQ.FASTA 4 2000-1月 "write_fingerprint" "write_fingerprint"
.SH NAME
write_fingerprint \- make the sequence fingerprint data of the given nucleotide sequence
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIwrite_fingerprint(\fBfile\fR as <generic> FingerprintMatrixWriter, 
\fBseqs\fR as any, 
\fBdebug\fR as integer = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
make the sequence fingerprint data of the given nucleotide sequence 
 collection, and then write the generated fingerprint data into the target 
 fingerprint matrix file
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfile\fB \fR\- 
 a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.OperonMapper.FingerprintMatrixWriter\fR object that is created by the 
 \fBopen.fingerprint_writer\fR api.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBseqs\fB \fR\- 
 a nucleotide fasta sequence collection for make the sequence fingerprint 
 data, which can be a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.FastaFile\fR object, a collection of the 
 @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.FastaSeq\fR object, or a character vector of the raw sequence 
 data.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdebug\fB \fR\- 
 only make the fingerprint data of the first n sequence for debug test? a 
 negative value means that all of the input sequence will be processed.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the input @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.OperonMapper.FingerprintMatrixWriter\fR object, so that this api can 
 be used in a pipeline manner;
 
 this function returns a R# error message object if the input sequence data 
 can not be cast to a fasta sequence collection.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the fasta headers title of the input sequence data should be formatted as: 
 \fB{gb_acc}.{locus_tag} {left} {right} {strand}|{biom_string}\fR, the 
 \fBstrand\fR token should be \fBforward\fR or \fBreverse\fR, or the target 
 sequence will be skipped with a warning message.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bioseq.fasta
.SH FILES
.PP
seqtoolkit.dll
.PP
